heartsim default anatomy pack — baked from open, CC BY 4.0 meshes

HEART
Rodero C, Strocchi M, Marciniak M, Longobardi S, Whitaker J, O'Neill MD, Gillette K, Augustin C,
Plank G, Vigmond EJ, Lamata P, Niederer SA. Virtual cohort of extreme and average four-chamber
heart meshes from statistical shape model (v1.0.0). Zenodo, 2021. doi:10.5281/zenodo.4593739
(file average.tar.gz). Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
Paper: Rodero C et al. Linking statistical shape models and simulated function in the healthy
adult human heart. PLoS Comput Biol 2021;17(4):e1008851. doi:10.1371/journal.pcbi.1008851
Changes by heartsim: the `average` mesh was re-oriented to the measured long-axis pose
(Engblom 2005 / Kayyali 2025, Narumi 2022), re-centred on the ventricular centroid, its tagged
boundary surfaces extracted, smoothed and decimated, its myocardium resampled to a 2.3 mm cell
cloud with the dataset's fibres and universal ventricular coordinates; vessel tubes beyond the
cropped inlets, an appendage body, the coronary sinus, the conduction system, atrial sub-regions,
AHA segments and landmarks were added by rule (heartsim-geometry, MIT OR Apache-2.0).

TORSO
Qian S, Monaci S, Mendonca-Costa C, Campos F, Gemmell P, Zaidi S, Rajani R, Whitaker J,
Rinaldi CA, Bishop MJ. Whole Torso Computational Models (v1.0). King's College London, Zenodo,
2022. doi:10.5281/zenodo.7253863 (file KCL_torso1.zip). Licence: Creative Commons Attribution
4.0 International, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
Changes by heartsim: the outer skin surface of torso 1 was extracted from the tetrahedral model,
closed at the CT's cut planes, smoothed, decimated, scaled uniformly about the subject's own
ventricular centroid to the heart's left-ventricular length and translated into the heart frame;
the electrode sites were placed on it by rule; every other tag was discarded.

The pack as a whole is distributed under CC BY 4.0 for the geometry derived from the two sources
above; heartsim's own additions are MIT OR Apache-2.0.
Nothing from any proprietary program or data set was used.
